Message-ID: <bgBYxNPYMm8.sd7oYrwABAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <bgBYxNPYMm8.I0yqqIpVBgAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <bgBYxNPYMm8.I0yqqIpVBgAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/bgBYxNPYMm8/m/sd7oYrwABAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the stress/normal indicator as an additive covariate in scanone(), you’re assuming that QTL have the same effect in both conditions, but that there is an overall shift in the mean response.

Probably what you want is to treat it as an interactive covariate, with the argument intcovar. Then the effects of QTL vary between the two conditions.

karl

